                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a0f6d879-65b8-39a8-8706-983d9cb02705",
                        "entry_id": "31a48763-48de-3cb1-92af-10eaccffd5f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lacking trust; untrusting."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "119511a6-dcba-352b-b68d-5e62bc385898",
                        "entry_id": "31a48763-48de-3cb1-92af-10eaccffd5f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Which does not need any trust, or a trusted third party."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe21f5b4-26cf-4b93-9371-63e5d16a0f4b",
                                "sense_id": "119511a6-dcba-352b-b68d-5e62bc385898",
                                "text": "A trustless network can run even if none of its nodes trusts another."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26c37c0f-feb9-493d-9c1a-48cb1038aa64",
                                "sense_id": "119511a6-dcba-352b-b68d-5e62bc385898",
                                "text": "In the trustless cryptocurrency world, you can still trust the cryptocurrency community and its mechanisms to ensure that the blockchain contains an accurate and immutable—unchangeable—record of cryptocurrency transactions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9730acc4-8819-4035-903c-3a2d436c19c6",
                                "sense_id": "119511a6-dcba-352b-b68d-5e62bc385898",
                                "text": "This article draws from the extensive academic discussion on the concepts of “trust” and “confidence” to argue that blockchain technology is not a ‘trustless technology’ but rather a ‘confidence machine’."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a14758fb-f26a-45da-bf59-782a72bc4516",
                                "sense_id": "119511a6-dcba-352b-b68d-5e62bc385898",
                                "text": "If it becomes cheaper to use a TTP to verify the transaction than some cryptographic or other automated mechanism, then the benefit of being “trustless” becomes an illusion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0b467a8-fe80-4498-8b3e-f1414597bdf0",
                                "sense_id": "119511a6-dcba-352b-b68d-5e62bc385898",
                                "text": "And the system would be “trustless” — that is, it would not rely on a trusted party, such as a bank or government, to arbitrate transactions."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b6e788c3-bcbc-35a4-a531-1c469feb9d30",
                        "entry_id": "31a48763-48de-3cb1-92af-10eaccffd5f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Untrustworthy; not deserving to be trusted."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "180a2480-9b01-4a60-8c79-2530a028d77e",
                                "sense_id": "b6e788c3-bcbc-35a4-a531-1c469feb9d30",
                                "text": "But thinks it not that[…]the voice which the spirit uttereth when he is gone from man[…]is a voice proceeding from the spirit which is in earthly, ignorant, and overclouded man; and therefore a trustles and not to be-believed voice?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
